{"id": "EUVD-2026-102992", "enisaUuid": "df5ef749-68c3-3cc3-88f7-a0933e85d748", "description": "OtterMind Nubase through 0.1.4 contains a missing authentication vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to access private bucket objects because /storage/v1/object/{bucketId}/{path} is treated as public for every HTTP method. Attackers knowing a tenant subdomain, bucket id and object path can download objects from private buckets and delete stored objects without an apikey or JWT.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:16:58", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/nubase-storage-private-object-unauth-download", "https://github.com/OtterMind/Nubase/blob/v0.1.4/src/main/java/ai/nubase/common/multitenancy/UnifiedMultiTenancyFilter.java#L363-L379", "https://github.com/OtterMind/Nubase/blob/v0.1.4/src/main/java/ai/nubase/auth/controller/storage/StorageObjectReadController.java#L68-L74", "https://github.com/OtterMind/Nubase/blob/v0.1.4/src/main/java/ai/nubase/auth/service/StorageService.java#L176-L200", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ottermind-nubase-through-0.1.4-missing-authentication-in-storage-object-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4jxc-c3cr-q9xx", "CVE-2026-111701"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c109879-8625-39cf-ae5e-0a7e2b5b7fa0", "product": {"name": "Nubase", "vendor": {"name": "OtterMind"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b099c352-a276-3aa1-a729-1a5a5a08f62b", "vendor": {"name": "OtterMind"}}], "isExploited": false}